/F2+0 6.75000 Tf
13.50000 TL
( Muscles produce creatinine\054 a waste product\054 from creatine phosphate\054 a substance that stores a lot of energy\056 Unlike urea\054 the amount of creatinine) Tj
T*
(generated is constant and mostly depends on muscle mass\056 Age\054 gender\054 race\054 muscularity\054 exercise\054 pregnancy\054 and several other physiological characteristics can) Tj
T*
(all have an impact on serum creatinine levels\056 Decreased serum Creatinine is associated with increasing Age and poor muscle mass\054 such as muscular atrophy\056 Both) Tj
T*
(acute and chronic renal disease and blockage are associated with elevated blood creatinine levels\056 Creatinine is not an appropriate indicator for identifying kidney) Tj
T*
(disease in its early stages since an increase in blood creatinine is only seen when there is significant nephron damage\056) Tj
